# secrets — never commit real API keys/contact emails
.env

# source PDFs and raw API cache: large (~3GB combined), regenerable from the
# arxiv_id/doi/url fields already in data/context_sok.db and the Excel exports,
# and PDFs carry their own redistribution terms — not part of the distilled
# knowledge deliverable. Re-fetch via scripts/ + config.yaml if ever needed.
data/papers/
data/cache/
data/*.log

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# rebuilt harness venv (vllm + torch, ~10GB, regenerable -- see agentdojo_harness/README.md)
agentdojo_harness/.venv/

# third-party attack/defense source clones (own git history, their own
# licenses, regenerable). The MANIFEST is ours and is tracked: it pins every
# clone to the commit our runs used, and scripts/setup_third_party.py fetches
# and verifies them from it.
third_party/*
!third_party/MANIFEST.json

# verification packets: large derived artifacts, rebuilt by
# scripts/build_packets.py in seconds. The workbooks are tracked; the zips
# (24-55 MB each) exist to hand to reviewers once, not to live in history.
verification/packets/*.zip

# source PDFs of surveyed papers, wherever they land. Same rule as
# data/papers/ above: they carry their own redistribution terms and this repo
# is public. 81 of them had slipped past the data/papers/ rule by living
# somewhere else. Every one is recoverable from the DOI/arXiv id kept with its
# record; MANUAL_PDF_WORKLIST.md lists the ones that need a browser session.
# Our OWN figures (latex/figures, paper_kit/figures) are not affected.
verification/packets/*/pdfs/
data/source_pdfs_manual/

# contribution-screen bundles: copies of gitignored PDFs
data/exports/contribution_screen/bundles/

# the confidence-group key: sending it to a coder biases the study it tests
data/exports/confidence_validation/_key_DO_NOT_SHARE.json

# meeting decks: internal, and regenerable from the registries by
# scripts/build_advisor_deck.py and scripts/build_presentation.py. They are
# ours, so this is tidiness rather than licensing - a public artifact repo
# should hold the artifact, not the slides we showed each other.
advisor_meeting.pptx
advisor_meeting.pdf
context_sok_results_presentation.pptx
context_sok_results_presentation.pdf
